## T8 — The room description modal

**File:** `src/routes/app/rooms/[id]/__tests__/page.svelte.test.ts` *(new)* — Pattern C.

- `it('does not show the description in the page body')` — it lives in the modal now.
- `it('opens the description modal when the room name is clicked')`
- `it('renders the room name as the modal title')`
- `it('shows the full, unclamped description in the modal')`
- `it('shows a placeholder for a room with no description')`
- `it('shows the location in the modal when set')`
- `it('shows the member count in the modal')`
- `it('makes the room name a real button, not a clickable div')` — assert `getByRole('button')`
  finds it. Keyboard and screen-reader access come free from the right element; the existing
  `.person` `<div onclick>` cards are a wart, not a pattern to copy.
- `it('keeps the owner edit form separate from the description modal')` — clicking the name must not
  open the editor, and clicking `edit` must not open the modal.
- `it('shows a mute control for a member')`
- `it('shows no mute control for a non-member')`

